Z||000002||Cheever2||12-06-2000||08:42 PM||||It's obviously not going to be a street-legal project.  What are your intentions: racing (drags, ovals, road courses, terrorizing the local BMXers), shows (World of Wheels, local Cruise-ins, Annie's Hub Cap City), prototype concept-car (for GM, Tyco, John Deere), or just your own personal hobby interests (gang alternative, keeping away from the local bully, chasing cats, not smart enough for model rocketry)?<P>Looks like a fairly rigid suspension there.  I'd recommend springs & shocks.  Not much of a safety program in your garage either, I suspect.  Front-engine designs for karts went out years ago, glad to see somebody's bringing it back, but I wouldn't want to be sitting there when that blower goes.  Might want to consider some body 'glass for improved aerodynamics; better yet, get that software for wind tunnel simulation.<P>If you're thinking of selling it to NASA for their next Mars rover, they'll need a driver: take my son, please.<BR> ||||reg||1
