Z||000005||zeusrekning||12-06-2000||10:20 PM||||I am into strange things.<BR>I like to build any thing and everthing motorized with wheels.<BR>I got the mower from a friend.I liked it because it was tiny.<BR>Then i got a 1971 honda cb350/four<BR>(tiny bore and stroke)both less than 2 inches i think.)<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wizard_1.jpg"> <P>look at the flywheel cover on the ground to compare the size of the mower.<P>Projects i have started designing or  thinking about.<BR>1.Go kart with fully independent supension<BR>2.my mower<BR>3.golf cart using same suspension as the go-kart for track use.<BR>4.Small motorcycle powered rail(like a junior dragster)<P>My intentions?<BR>I will take it to my local 1/8 mile and run it if they'll let me.<BR>Want to do hella wheel spins.<BR>and just get looks if i take it to our fiero show next year.<BR>I would love to build "custom toys" for a living. <BR>Just some one come up and tell me they want a golf cart to take hunting but don't want a four wheeler then build it.<BR>If you guys a really interested I can tell you my plans for the mower.<BR>I just drew a pic to scale then added the guy to goof off.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Seanh||12-08-2000||08:03 AM||||One of my Friends at school had a SBC 305 engine on a golf cart. Man, that thing was awesome. It hauled like nothin' before. It had a custom suspension and 18" off road tires. We took it up to the lake once and drove it around on the beach and the off road trail, you wouldnt believe how many looks we got with that thing. Finally, after driveing it across the beach for about 4 hours, the Game & Parks officer told us we had to stop, because it wasnt a licenced vehical, he even looked it over for about 30 Min. before leaving. Needless to say, it really got alot of attention when we DID take it to the gold course and use it. We even drove it into a shallow lake to get our ball back, people had the strangest look on their faces. I would like to do a Go-Kart project some day, like with a 3.1 V6 maybe. I think a big ol' V8 would be a little over kill.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
